A||N||9||fropuff||Looking for info on RSM flush-mounts||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||01-21-2001||03:28 PM||||Hey, I am thinking of getting some flush-mounted headlights for my 86 GT.  I've been looking at all the ones that are out there, and I conclude that I like RSMs the best.  Coincidently, they're also the most expensive.  I think this is where I need to make my own.  I know how I would do it anyway.  What I'm looking for is info on the lights that they use.  There are four of them, and they are bigger than on Tom's kit.  I'm also wondering if there's any other information on the size of stuff.  Actually I only need to know what kind of lights they are and the size of them.  If you're looking for a picture, it's at:  <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/light.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/light.jpg</A>   These are awesome!  Thanks for any help.  Oh yeah: can I do a cover for them too?  I don't like the look of them; I want to keep the lines on the hood and all.  I could do my own.  Can I use glass, or lexan, or what?  I'm thinking of the ones on the 90s 300ZX.  What material are those covers made out of?  Thanks again for any help.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||10
Z||000001||fropuff||01-21-2001||04:31 PM||||A close-up picture, if available, would be greatly appreciated also.  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||01-21-2001||05:23 PM||||I just went out and took the covers off.  I don't know how big those lights are, but they sure don't look like they'll fit.  Any idea?  The only ones that look like they'll fit is Tom's kit.  Any idea?  Anybody have the RSM email? Thanks.  I'm not being impatient either.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||01-21-2001||07:23 PM||||Unless it's a single bulb, I don't really like the recessed lights. Call me old-fashioned, but I love popups.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Also the new style.. but not the older style lights with separate bulbs etc...<P>As for your question, it's possible that Tom's kit and the RSM one use similar lights.. I'm pretty sure the rest of the kit is the same style. (metal bucket, some brackets, etc...)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000004||Formula||01-21-2001||10:45 PM||||I think the rsm kit is a photo edit.  Im sure they make one but I'd get more pics then that one to go by.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||01-21-2001||10:45 PM||||I don't know if those are the same lights; might just be the angle of the camera **** .  If they are the same lights, first of all, I won't get them.  I saw an up-close picture of Tom's kit, and I don't like them.  Sorry if I offended anyone, but that's my personal opinion.  Secondly, if they are the same kit, RSM is the biggest ripoff ever.  $500 for those lights!  If anyone has some information, I would still like to hear it.  I like the looks of RSMs lights.  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||01-21-2001||10:47 PM||||Formula: might be a editing job.  I don't want to get the RSM kit, just some information on what lights they used.  I would rather save my 500 frickin dollars and get some nitrous thank you very much!  I emailed RSM and asked what lights they used; hope they reply.  Thanks for the heads-up!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||01-22-2001||12:02 AM||||After seeing what goes into the kit, you'd think almost any price was a ripoff.. unless you're not skilled with metal working, as a lot of people aren't. But it's just sheet metal, brackets, etc.. the wiring should be the same for the lights themselves.. all you'd need to do is make new connectors for the replacement (camaro?) bulbs, and put them in brackets..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000008||KEV||01-22-2001||10:23 AM||||HEY FROPUFF, THE KIT SOLD BY TOM'S ASS. IS VERY MUCH THE SAMES AS RSM'S BUT THREE TIMES AS CHEAP IN PRICE TOM BUILDS AS NEEDED SO QUALITY IS FAR BETTER BECAUSE I ORDERED A SET FROM HIM AND DR RODEY ALSO AS A SET ON HIS 88 FORMULA CONV. AND HE WILL ALSO AGREE THAT THEY ARE VERY GOOD. SO SAVE FOR MONEY AND GET THEM FROM TOM YOU'LL BE HAPPY WITH THEM. JUST MY $.02||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||01-22-2001||03:16 PM||||FYI, the short form for accessories is Acc. not ASS.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>hehe..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
